comments.body:
Methinks I understand what causes that. [Here](https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/blob/f3351f4f75dd1dc43f8808235553593bf87e68a0/zellij-server/src/tab/copy_command.rs#L21) command spawned unconditionally and never waits for process exit via `.wait()` or `.wait_with_output()`. Exiting scope leaves child process in zombie state. Checked on minimal example to confirm that.
If we write to child process stdio and attempt to wait for it in the same thread it's gonna hang.  It looks like [the correct way](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/index.html#handling-io) to write to child's stdio via `write`/`write_all` is to take child's stdio and write to it in separate thread. Roughly new shape of the [function](https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/blob/f3351f4f75dd1dc43f8808235553593bf87e68a0/zellij-server/src/tab/copy_command.rs#L20):
```rust
pub fn set(&self, value: String) -> Result<()> {
    let mut process = Command::new(self.command.clone())
        .args(self.args.clone())
        .stdin(Stdio::piped())
        .spawn()
        .with_context(|| format!("couldn't spawn {}", self.command))?;
    // extract child's stdin
    let mut stdin = process
        .stdin
        .take()
        .context("could not get stdin")?;
    // important to pass it to the thread for some reason
    std::thread::spawn(move ||{
        stdin
        .write_all(value.as_bytes())
        .expect("couldn't write to  stdin");
    });
    // don't leave child in zombie state by forgetting it
    process
        .wait()
        .with_context(format!("failed to wait child process for {}", self.command)?;

    Ok(())
}
```
The other way around this is pass value as `.args` and remove buffer writing part completely. Of course call any wait function in either case. 

Also reference to [Child](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/struct.Child.html#warning) warns about handling child state.

Force kill after 1 sec aren't really correct solution, though looks like it works and copy commands usually do not take that long. 
@participant1 @participant3 can you check if it fixed issue for you as well? 
0.43.0 at 4ee376e2d75a67ad works for me.
